WEBVTT

00:44:57.943 --> 00:45:00.143
That was just -- no matter
what else he said,

00:45:00.167 --> 00:45:04.020
that was beyond the pale
and could be someplace we could never go.

00:45:04.044 --> 00:45:06.684
So it's been awkward.

00:45:06.708 --> 00:45:10.702
And for a lot of people whose policy
ideas find a natural home

00:45:10.726 --> 00:45:12.140
in the Republican Party,

00:45:12.164 --> 00:45:14.025
it's not clear what's going to happen,

00:45:14.049 --> 00:45:16.138
because the Republican
Party, I don't think,

00:45:16.162 --> 00:45:17.887
is not going back to the way it was,

00:45:17.911 --> 00:45:21.541
and it may be caught up in Trumpianism
for a good while to come.

00:45:21.565 --> 00:45:23.323
And -- I'll just speak for myself --

00:45:23.347 --> 00:45:25.743
I just feel homeless,
politically homeless.

00:45:25.767 --> 00:45:27.942
I actually like
Elizabeth Warren personally,

00:45:27.966 --> 00:45:29.986
but I never agree with her ideas.